IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hpr-law`
IMPORT `hpr-seat`

-- Health Practitioner Regulation (Adoption of National Law) Act 2009 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question
-- of the complainant's seat (hpr-seat.l4) and the shared rules in hpr-law.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `complainant cases`

`d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY

`now` MEANS `registered under the National Law now`
`former` MEANS `formerly registered under the National Law`
`prior only` MEANS `registered only under a corresponding prior Act, never under the National Law`
`UPC ground` MEANS `unsatisfactory professional conduct or professional misconduct`
`no provision` MEANS `the Act does not provide for this complaint on these facts`
`care below` MEANS `care, skill or judgment significantly below the standard reasonably expected of an equivalent practitioner`
`referral` MEANS `referring or recommending while having a financial interest in it`
`urgent` MEANS `a doctor refusing or failing without reasonable cause to attend a person believed to need urgent attention`
`council meeting` MEANS `the Council at an inquiry at a Council meeting`
`PSC` MEANS `a Professional Standards Committee`
`AC` MEANS `an Assessment Committee`
`lawyer` MEANS `entitled to attend and to be represented by an Australian legal practitioner, or by another adviser with leave`
`other ground` MEANS `another ground (competence, impairment, a conviction, suitability)`
`no further action` MEANS `decided that no further action should be taken`

§§ `ss 139G, 139H, 144, 144B -- can I complain`

-- Arguments: registration, ground, about behaviour while registered, the prior Act allowed it.
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `now` `UPC ground` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: any person can make this complaint`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `now` `an impairment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: any person can make this complaint`
-- A ground s 144 does not list.
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `now` `something else` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no provision`
-- s 139G: a former registrant, about behaviour while registered, and about later behaviour.
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `former` `a criminal conviction or criminal finding for an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, about the practitioner's behaviour while registered`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `former` `an impairment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no provision`
-- s 139H(3): only to the extent the prior Act allowed.
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `prior only` `not competent to practise the profession` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, about behaviour while registered under the prior Act, to the extent that Act allowed`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `prior only` `not competent to practise the profession` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the prior Act would not have allowed this complaint`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `prior only` `not competent to practise the profession` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no provision`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `never registered` `UPC ground` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no provision`

§§ `ss 144C-144E -- lodging`

#ASSERT `How do I lodge my complaint` `a Council` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `lodge it with the Council's Executive Officer: it can be referred once lodged`
#ASSERT `How do I lodge my complaint` `the Health Care Complaints Commission` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `lodge it with the Commission under s 9 of the Health Care Complaints Act 1993: it can be referred once lodged`
#ASSERT `How do I lodge my complaint` `a Council` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `lodge it with the Council's Executive Officer: it may be looked into, but cannot be referred until it is in writing with the particulars of the allegations`
#ASSERT `How do I lodge my complaint` `the Health Care Complaints Commission` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `lodge it with the Commission under s 9 of the Health Care Complaints Act 1993: it may be looked into, but cannot be referred until it is in writing with the particulars of the allegations`

§§ `s 139B(2) -- financial interest (shared rule)`

-- Arguments: provider, percentage, private interest, partner, prescribed.
#ASSERT `has a financial interest` `a public company` 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `has a financial interest` `a public company` 4.99 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `has a financial interest` `a private company` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `has a financial interest` `a natural person` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `has a financial interest` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `has a financial interest` `another kind of provider or supplier` 50 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 139B-139D -- unsatisfactory professional conduct`

-- Arguments: profession, conduct, provider, percentage, private interest, partner, prescribed, disclosed, other doctor.
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `care below` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 139B(1)(i) with (2)(a): 5% exactly is enough; just under is not, and then no head is met (open list: NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `another registered health profession` `referral` `a public company` 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `another registered health profession` `referral` `a public company` 4.99 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Disclosed before or at the time: the "unless" is met.
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `another registered health profession` `referral` `a public company` 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `pharmacy` `referral` `a private company` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `pharmacy` `referral` `a private company` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `referral` `a natural person` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `referral` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `referral` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 139C(c): unless the doctor took all reasonable steps to have another attend.
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `urgent` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `urgent` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 139C heads reach medical practitioners only; s 139D heads pharmacists only.
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `nursing and midwifery` `a doctor convicted of an offence listed in s 139C(a)` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `pharmacy` `a pharmacist in charge not displaying their name and "PHARMACIST IN CHARGE"` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `medical` `a pharmacist supplying precursor drugs unnecessarily or excessively` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `another registered health profession` `overservicing: a service that was unnecessary, not reasonably required or excessive` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could it be unsatisfactory professional conduct` `another registered health profession` `none of these` `another kind of provider or supplier` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 139E -- professional misconduct`

-- Arguments: profession, conduct, disclosed, had a financial interest, other doctor, serious enough.
