§§ `ss 147B(3), 147C(7), 148I, 150(6A), 150A(6), 150B(2) -- my civil claim`

#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `a finding of a Council at an inquiry at a Council meeting` FALSE EQUALS `admissible as evidence in any legal proceedings`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `advice an Assessment Committee obtained` FALSE EQUALS `not admissible in my civil claim, and no one can be made to produce it or give evidence about it`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `advice an Assessment Committee obtained` TRUE EQUALS `usable, because the Council has ordered otherwise`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `a skills-testing report to an Assessment Committee` TRUE EQUALS `no one can be required to produce it or reveal its contents in civil proceedings`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `the Council's written reasons for urgent suspension or conditions (s 150)` FALSE EQUALS `not admissible in court proceedings (other than under the National Law) or at an inquest`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `the Council's written reasons on a review of urgent action (s 150A)` FALSE EQUALS `not admissible in court proceedings (other than under the National Law) or at an inquest`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `an audio recording or transcript of a Council meeting about urgent action (s 150B)` FALSE EQUALS `not admissible in court proceedings (other than under the National Law) or at an inquest`
#ASSERT `Can it be used in my civil claim` `another document or finding` FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not say`
